#X obj 60 528 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Arguments 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 552 name: the [text define -k name] that holds the values \; (it lives in the main patch and is saved with it), f 64;
#X obj 60 612 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Inlets 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 636 0: messages from the voice's outlet 1 ('dump ...') \; 1: slot number 0-15 \, e.g. from an [hradio], f 64;
#X obj 60 696 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Outlets 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 720 0: to the voice inlet (restores values \, asks for dumps) \; 1: loaded values as a list v0 v1 ... for number boxes, f 64;
#X obj 60 780 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Wiring 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 804 voice outlet 1 -> skpreset inlet 0 \; skpreset outlet 0 -> voice inlet \; [hradio] or step counter -> skpreset inlet 1 \; Several voices: one [text define -k name] and one \; [skpreset name] each \, and feed all slot inlets from one \; [hradio] to switch the whole kit per step., f 64;
#X obj 60 928 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty How\ a\ slot\ change\ works 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 952 1 The current slot is written (the voice is asked for a dump). \; 2 The new slot is selected. \; 3 Its line is loaded into the voice. An empty slot keeps the \; current sound and is filled with it. \; Edits are therefore kept per slot \, like step locks., f 64;
#X obj 60 1060 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty The\ text 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1084 One line per slot \, line number = slot number. Double-click \; [text define] to edit it\; 'write file' and 'read file' save \; or load a bank. A line only loads into its own voice type \; (trxb2 into trxb2~). '-' marks an empty slot., f 64;
#X text 82 1176 Credits: idea and first patch by Peter \; Pd wrapper skandrums-pd (CC0) \, built with Claude (Anthropic) \; Part of skandrums-pd \, see the voice help files, f 64;
